  "problem": "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}{q}_{11} & {q}_{12} \\\\ {q}_{21} & {q}_{22} \\\\ {q}_{31} & {q}_{32}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{\u23de}{[\\begin{aligned}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. Given that the columns ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ of $A$ are orthogonal, and that the columns ${q}_{1},{q}_{2}$ of $Q$ were obtained by normalizing the columns of $A,$ what is the value of ${q}_{11}\\cdot {r}_{22}?$",
